🐛 Describe the bug
Unable to get attributes from Dataset class.
How to reproduce:
from torch.utils.data import Dataset

class MyDataset(Dataset):
    def __init__(self):
       self.n = 10

   def __getitem__(self, index):
       return index

    def __len__(self):
        return self.n

ds = MyDataset()
print(ds.n)
This would rase AttributeError.
What I found
I found that Dataset only supports for getting functions since 1.10, because the __getattr__ function is overloaded.
Is this a bug or feature?
    def __getattr__(self, attribute_name):
        if attribute_name in Dataset.functions:
            function = functools.partial(Dataset.functions[attribute_name], self)
            return function
        else:
            raise AttributeError
Versions
PyTorch 1.10
